  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_cornet_cb8ad7cb0fe9e3752188ac5bd51c2ea8ddc8b600a0c45a810d8b6be8fc208d43a4">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>Term applied to women's headdresses which vary in style from the 14th to the 18th century, but which are often of conical shape and usually made of delicate materials with lappets of lace or ribbon. [Source: Getty AAT]</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
